I'd only been playing Nethack seriously for about a month before I
ascended my first character (Valkyrie) yesterday.  It would not have
been possible without Mark Johnson's Maniac's Ascension Guide, Eva
Myers' list of Nethack Spoilers, David Damerell's NetHack Object
Identification Spoiler, Krysia's Krusader's story of Ellora, and all of
the other spoilers.  Thanks to the Dev Team for developing such a
remarkable game.

I suspected this try was exceptional when quaffing from a fountain
produced a friendly water demon.  I wished for a blessed +2 gray dragon
scale mail, which helped tremendously.

I got a bag of holding from Sokoban, and found three more during the
game! I accidentally put on inside the other, and, boom, both
disappeared with their contents.  I was a little bummed out, but, in
hindsight, it was the best thing that could have happened, because the
bags were very likely to keep me burdened.

A little later, my pet cat stepped on a polymorph trap and turned into
a winged gargoyle.  The winged gargoyle really helped by killing
shopkeepers for me.  I made sure to keep him away from Izchak.  It was
a shame that I had to kill my pet, after leaving him on the Quest Home
level and allowing him to become peaceful.  I tried to make him tame
again by throwing a tripe ration towards him, but that angered him.  He
put up a good fight.

It was my first time ever making it to the Quest level.  I had to quaff
a blessed potion of gain level to get to experience level 14 to enter
the Quest.  I had considered visiting Medusa first, but I could not
find any means of levitating.  I used a couple of scrolls of create
earth to attempt to reach her, but I soon decided to try the Quest
first.

I had received Mojo before the Quest, thanks to a bag of tricks and an
altar.  I quickly blessed and echanted the hammer.  It would take me
all the way to the end.

My firts big mistake resulted from hunger.  I was hungry, so I killed a
few wolves and ate them, except that one of them wasn't a wolf: it was
a werejackal.  'You'll pay for this!'  I turned into a werejackal, and
had to drop all of my armor and weapons.  I slinked off to a shop,
where I waited about 100 turns to see if I might get better.  I decided
to risk praying, and, as my god was well-pleased, he returned me to
human form.  I tried to get back to my stash, but ran into a panther.
He took my HP down very quickly.  I had eaten a tengu and a nymph, so I
managed to get teleport and teleport control.  I teleported over to the
stash (it took me two tries to get it right.)  I wore my armor, wielded
my weapon, and slew the panther.  I took much greater care with eating
after that (although I did mistakenly eat a soldier in the Castle,
right before my ascension run.)

I found a Wand of Wishing before the Castle, and wished for boots of
levitation (to get to Medusa, where I found another pair), a magic
marker, and, later, a shield of reflection, gauntlets of power, and 2
blessed scrolls of charging.

Medusa quickly fell victim to her reflection, and the Castle proved
little difficulty as well.  The Castle Wand of Wishing got me a blessed
magic marker, which yielded 5 scrolls of enchant armor on a single
charge.  I also got a couple of amulets of life saving from it, too.

The next big scare came from Orcus town.  I fell through Orcus Town,
and came back up the stairs.  I smacked Orcus with Mojo, and he fled to
the upstairs.  I was starting to chase him when he appeared next to me
with his friend Demogorgon!  I thought I was wearing speed boots, as I
had read in the Armor Spoiler by Kevin Hugo and Dylan O'Donnell that
combat boots were speed boots.  It turned out they were boots of Water
Walking.  =(  I couldn't keep up with healing myself from Demogorgon's
sickness attacks.  I died, but was wearing an Amulet of Life Saving.  I
quickly zapped my Wand of Wishing and wished for another Amulet of Life
Saving, but I barely had time to put it on before I died again.

With my HP quickly draining (28 HP and no Amulet of Life Saving), I
realized I needed to escape.  I tried to make my way back to the
stairs, slowed by the swarm of summoned monsters.  I managed to make it
down to the the next level, but was followed by Yeenoghu.  I hit him
once or twice with my hammer, and once he was gone, I used the time to
heal myself and wish for another Amulet of Life Saving.

I used my blessed scroll of genocide on Dragons, as they were nicely
represented among the summoned monsters.  I had already genocide liches
and mind flayers.  I left Orcus and Demogorgon alone until I could
formulate a plan.  I came across a third Wand of Wishing, and wished
for speed boots and blessed wax candles (Izchak only had 4.)  I spent
my time beneath Orcus and Demogorgon continuing my campaign to cut
paths beteewn the up and down stairs.  While I was one level below
Orcus and Demogorgon, a pit fiend summoned monsters around me.  A
cockatrice was among them.  I quickly killed it and raced back up the
stairs, dropping one of my bags of holding to make sure I was
unburdened.

