I continued down through Gehennom, reaching the Vibrating Square.  I
visited Rodney and stoned him with a cockatrice corpse.  (I didn't see
him again until I reached the Plane of Earth, where I zapped him with a
Wand of Death.)

I invoked the Orb of Fate to level teleport to the Vibrating Square,
and ended up five spaces away from it!

On the Planes, I used my crystal ball to find the portals.  The
elemental Planes were uneventful.  On the Astral Plane, though, I ran
into Pestilence.  I know now that he should be put off until last.  It
took three zaps of the Wand of Death to kill him.  After I killed him a
few times, I realized that I had to try to outrun him.  I made it to
one of the altars, only to discover it was an alter to Loki, and not
Odin!  I killed Pestilence again, and ran to another door to try to
find the altar.

I allowed a couple of weak creatures to beat up on me to gain time, as
I attempted to wrest one last zap from a Wand of Wishing.  (I had
another wish from another Wand of Wishing, but I wanted to save the
guaranteed wish for an emergency.)  I had hoped to get another Amulet
of Life Saving.  I gave up eventually.

I killed Famine with Mojo and rushed forward to the Altar.  It was
Odin's! My character was confused, so I applied a blessed unicorn horn
before I offered the amulet.  I hadn't read anything about sacrificing
the amulet while confused, but I wasn't taking any chances.

Phew!

